================================================================================
TOOL DESIGN AND MULTI-AGENT ORCHESTRATION - QUICK GUIDE
================================================================================

CORE IDEA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A single AI agent managing too many tools can become unreliable.

Better approach:
- Design reliable tools
- Use orchestration patterns
- Split complex work across specialist agents
- Add monitoring, quality gates, and failure handling


================================================================================
1. ROBUST TOOL API DESIGN
================================================================================

An agent is only as reliable as its tools.

Good Tool Contract:
- Clear purpose
- Precise input schema
- Predictable output schema
- Clear error handling

HTTP Errors:
- 400 = Bad Request -> Don't retry
- 404 = Not Found -> Don't retry
- 429 = Rate Limit -> Retry with backoff
- 504 = Timeout -> Retry

Idempotency:
- Prevents duplicate operations during retries
- Critical for payments, transactions, and account creation

Testing:
- Test complete tool workflows before agent deployment


================================================================================
2. TOOL ORCHESTRATION PATTERNS
================================================================================

1. SEQUENTIAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tool A -> Tool B -> Tool C

Use when one step depends on the previous step.

Example:
Validate Identity -> Create Account -> Send Email


2. PARALLEL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

             +-> Tool A -+
Input ------>+-> Tool B -+-> Aggregate -> Output
             +-> Tool C -+

Use when tasks are independent.

Benefits:
- Lower latency
- Faster processing

Handle:
- Result aggregation
- Partial failures
- Retries


3. CONDITIONAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input -> Validation
          |
     +----+----+
     |    |    |
     v    v    v
   Path A Path B Fallback

Use when workflow depends on business rules or validation.


REAL-WORLD COMBINATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Parallel Collection
      |
      v
Sequential Processing
      |
      v
Conditional Routing


================================================================================
3. MULTI-AGENT PATTERNS
================================================================================

PATTERN 1: SPECIALIST AGENT ENSEMBLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

             +-> Financial Agent --+
Input ------>+-> Risk Agent -------+-> Orchestrator -> Decision
             +-> Compliance Agent -+

Each specialist has:
- Clear responsibility
- Defined criteria
- Specific expertise

Orchestrator:
- Combines results
- Identifies agreements/disagreements
- Evaluates trade-offs

Decision Agent:
- Produces recommendation
- Confidence level
- Next steps


PATTERN 2: HIERARCHICAL ORCHESTRATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

                Orchestrator
                     |
          +----------+----------+
          |          |          |
          v          v          v
       Research   Analysis   Writing
          |          |          |
          +----------+----------+
                     |
                     v
              Progress Monitor
                     |
              +------+------+
              |             |
              v             v
         Aggregator     Failure Handler

Layers:

Strategy Layer:
- Orchestrator plans and delegates

Execution Layer:
- Specialist agents perform tasks

Coordination Layer:
- Monitor progress and quality

Best for:
Large enterprise workflows with many coordinated tasks.


PATTERN 3: RESEARCH -> CRITIQUE -> REFINE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Research Agent
      |
      v
Critic Agent
      |
      v
Quality Gate
      |
      +-> PASS -> Final Output
      |
      +-> FAIL -> Refine -> Re-evaluate

Research Agent:
- Collects information

Critic Agent:
- Checks accuracy, completeness, relevance

Refine Agent:
- Fixes identified gaps

Quality Gate:
- Controls pass/fail
- Prevents endless iteration


================================================================================
4. EDGE CASES AND AGENT DRIFT
================================================================================

Common Risks:
- Agent drift
- Unexpected inputs
- Hallucinations
- Tool failures

Prevention:
- Test edge cases
- Test adversarial inputs
- Monitor agent behavior
- Log actions and outputs
- Define clear goals and constraints
- Set measurable success criteria


================================================================================
5. TRANSLATING AI ARCHITECTURE TO BUSINESS VALUE
================================================================================

Don't explain only HOW the architecture works.

Explain WHY it matters.

Business Value:
- Reduce cost
- Reduce risk
- Improve response time
- Improve quality
- Accelerate delivery
- Create competitive advantage

Example:

Technical:
"Multiple specialist agents run in parallel."

Business:
"Independent analysis runs simultaneously, reducing response time."


Useful Analogies:

Multi-Agent System
= Team of specialists

Guardrails
= Compliance checks

Circuit Breaker
= Emergency shutdown mechanism


================================================================================
6. ENTERPRISE-GRADE AI PRINCIPLES
================================================================================

RELIABILITY
- Failure recovery
- Retries
- Graceful degradation

SAFETY
- Guardrails
- Sandboxing
- Circuit breakers

EXPLAINABILITY
- Logging
- Auditing
- Traceable decisions

These should be designed from the beginning, not added after failures.


================================================================================
QUICK REVISION
================================================================================

Sequential
-> A -> B -> C
-> Use when tasks depend on each other

Parallel
-> A + B + C simultaneously
-> Use for independent tasks

Conditional
-> IF condition -> Path A / Path B / Fallback
-> Use for business rules

Specialist Ensemble
-> Multiple experts -> Orchestrator -> Decision
-> Use for multidimensional problems

Hierarchical
-> Orchestrator -> Specialists -> Monitor -> Result
-> Use for large workflows

Research -> Critique -> Refine
-> Research -> Review -> Improve -> Quality Gate
-> Use when high-quality output is required


